    "updated_at": "2017-03-06T17:47:27Z",
    "body": "If it's not covered by specs, what is it covered by?  Something needs to define what happens to the session history on URL bar navigation....\r\n\r\nThe way this is implemented in practice, in Gecko, is that there's a security check, akin to the one that prevents the \"http: navigates to file:\" situation, that blocks the about:config load.  And clearly that check does not apply to loads via the URL bar.\r\n\r\nI should also note that the fetch spec has an explicit note saying \"about:config\" is handled in navigation, so either that note or the navigation spec is wrong.  ;)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
